  "origin": "peS2o (Pretraining Efficiently on S2ORC) is derived from S2ORC (Semantic Scholar Open Research Corpus), which aggregates academic papers with full text extracted from PDFs. peS2o v2 is released under ODC-By 1.0 (the same license as the S2ORC it derives from). ~57B tokens, 38.8M documents. The underlying papers carry heterogeneous licenses (arXiv papers under arXiv non-exclusive license or CC-BY; PubMed Central under various PMC licenses; publisher papers under subscription-access terms) — the per-document multi-license aggregate problem (Gap B) applies, but peS2o's dataset-level ODC-By license covers the curation/metadata, not the underlying paper texts. This record connects to the BLOOM/ROOTS S2ORC record: BLOOM/ROOTS used S2ORC directly (agreement-supplied, via the Semantic Scholar API), while OLMo/Dolma uses peS2o (a cleaned derivative, released under ODC-By). The two records document the same upstream source (S2ORC / Semantic Scholar) under two different downstream licenses (agreement-supplied vs. ODC-By) — a useful provenance-chain contrast for the same academic content. See notes/stress-test-olmo-dolma.md. peS2o is skewed towards STEM disciplines (per the Dolma datasheet's representativeness discussion).",
